[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Matterhorn Man]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.41]Lesson 3 | 第3课
[00:02.10]Matterhorn man | 马特霍恩山区人
[00:09.82]What was the main objective of early mountain climbers? | 早期登山者的主要目标是什么？
[00:15.30]Modern alpinists try to climb mountains by a route which will give them good sport, | 现代登山者总想找一条会给他们带来运动乐趣的路线登山上攀，
[00:21.93]and the more difficult it is, the more highly it is regarded. | 而且路线越是艰难，越会受到推崇。
[00:27.38]In the pioneering days however, this was not the case at all. | 然而在登山运动的初创时期，情况完全不是这样。
[00:33.65]The early climbers were looking for the easiest way to the top because the summit was the prize they sought, | 早期登山者所寻求的是通往顶峰的最容易的路线，因为山顶正是他们追求的目标，
[00:41.88]especially if it had never been attained before. | 尤其是以前从未有人登上过的顶峰。
[00:46.25]It is true that during their explorations they often faced difficulties and dangers of the most perilous nature, | 的确，在探险过程中，他们经常面临种种最危险性质的艰难险阻，
[00:55.54]equipped in a manner which would make a modern climber shudder at the thought, | 他们配备的装备足以让现代登山者一想到就胆战心惊，
[01:01.19]but they did not go out of their way to court such excitement. | 但他们并不是刻意去寻求这种刺激。
[01:05.87]They had a single aim, a solitary goal -- the top! | 他们只有一个目标，一个孤独的目标——山顶！
[01:12.55]It is hard for us to realize nowadays how difficult it was for the pioneers. | 如今我们很难理解当年的登山先驱是何等艰辛。
[01:19.21]Except for one or two places such as Zermatt and Chamonix, which had rapidly become popular. | 除了泽马特和夏蒙尼这样一两个很快出了名的地方，
[01:27.74]Alpine villages tended to be impoverished settlements cut off from civilization by the high mountains. | 阿尔卑斯山的山村往往是一些与文明隔绝的贫困居民点。
[01:36.40]Such inns as there were were generally dirty and flea-ridden; | 那时有的小旅店一般都肮脏不堪，跳蚤滋生；
[01:41.98]the food simply local cheese accompanied by bread often twelve months old, | 食物只是当地的干酪，配上往往存放了十二个月的面包，
[01:47.86]all washed down with coarse wine. | 人们就用劣质酒把这一切冲下肚去。
[01:51.85]Often a valley boasted no inn at all, and climbers found shelter wherever they could -- | 山谷里常常根本没有小旅店，登山者只能随遇而安地在任何能栖身的地方过夜——
[01:58.38]sometimes with the local priest (who was usually as poor as his parishioners), | 有时同当地牧师住在一起（他通常和他的教民一样穷），
[02:04.89]sometimes with shepherds or cheese-makers. | 有时同牧羊人或制干酪的人住在一起。
[02:08.72]Invariably the background was the same:dirt and poverty, and very uncomfortable. | 无论在哪里过夜，情况总是一样的：肮脏、贫穷，而且极不舒适。
[02:17.08]For men accustomed to eating seven-course dinners and sleeping between fine linen sheets at home, | 对于那些习惯于在家里一日七道菜、睡细布床单的人来说，
[02:24.66]the change to the Alps must have been very hard indeed. | 到阿尔卑斯山来的变化想必确实非常艰难。
